# PLAN3 DE1 — ooda bench in cmd_more.oo

File: openOODA/audit/plan3_de1.oot
Wave 1 WRITE. Own only `cli/cmd_more.oo`.

Logline: `run_ooda_bench` takes TimeCap, times a real oodac check with now_ms, and never prints `ooda bench: ok`.
Setup: Worktree `/home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-bench`. `host_run.oo` is read-only. DE2 owns `cli/main.oo`.
Beats:
  1. Replace the stub. New signature includes `&TimeCap`.
  2. Parse a non-flag file and optional `--run`. No file or missing file exits 2.
  3. Time `oodac check` (and optional `oodac run`) with `now_ms`. Do not call `run_oodac_check`.

## Signature

```
pub fn run_ooda_bench(fs: &FsCap, sys: &SysCap, time: &TimeCap, args: List[String])
```

args[0] is the word `bench`. The file is the first later token that does not start with `-`.

## Sample print

```
ooda bench: check fixtures/hello.oo 12ms
```

With `--run` after a passing check:

```
ooda bench: check fixtures/hello.oo 12ms
ooda bench: run fixtures/hello.oo 40ms
```

N is `t1 - t0` from `now_ms(time)`. If negative, 0. Letters `ms` have no space.

## Behavior on disk

  File: `cli/cmd_more.oo` (142 lines, limit 256).
  Imports: `find_compiler.oo`, `host_run.oo` for `find_oodac` / `find_src_root` / `sq` / `refuse_cli`.

  No file (`ooda bench`, or only flags including `--run`):
    `usage: ooda bench <file.oo> [--run]`
    `process_exit(2)`

  FILE absent:
    `ERR<TAB>bench<TAB>unreadable file: FILE`
    `process_exit(2)`

  Check fail:
    `ooda bench: check failed FILE`
    `process_exit(1)`
    No run line. No `ooda bench: ok`.

  Check ok:
    `ooda bench: check FILE Nms`
    `--run` only after check pass. Same command shape as `host_run.run_oodac`:
    `find_oodac` + `refuse_cli` + `find_src_root` +
    `sys_exec(sys, "sh", "-c", env + oodac + " check " + sq(path))`
    Optional run uses `" run "` instead of `" check "`.

  Timer is `now_ms(time)` only. No `date`. No bash timer.
  Did not call `run_oodac_check` (it `process_exit`s before ms can print).

